{"page":203,"verses":[{"verse_key":"9:100","surah":9,"ayah":100,"ar_uthmani":"وَٱلسَّـٰبِقُونَ ٱلْأَوَّلُونَ مِنَ ٱلْمُهَـٰجِرِينَ وَٱلْأَنصَارِ وَٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّبَعُوهُم بِإِحْسَـٰنٍ رَّضِىَ ٱللَّهُ عَنْهُمْ وَرَضُوا۟ عَنْهُ وَأَعَدَّ لَهُمْ جَنَّـٰتٍ تَجْرِى تَحْتَهَا ٱلْأَنْهَـٰرُ خَـٰلِدِينَ فِيهَآ أَبَدًا ۚ ذَٰلِكَ ٱلْفَوْزُ ٱلْعَظِيمُ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"God will be well pleased with the first emigrants and helpersand those who followed them in good deeds, and they will be well pleased with Him: He has prepared Gardens graced with flowing streams for them, there to remain for ever. That is the supreme triumph.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَٱلسَّـٰبِقُونَ","en_gloss":"And the forerunners","transliteration":"wal-sābiqūna","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱلْأَوَّلُونَ","en_gloss":"the first","transliteration":"l-awalūna","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":3,"ar":"مِنَ","en_gloss":"among","transliteration":"mina","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":4,"ar":"ٱلْمُهَـٰجِرِينَ","en_gloss":"the emigrants","transliteration":"l-muhājirīna","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":5,"ar":"وَٱلْأَنصَارِ","en_gloss":"and the helpers","transliteration":"wal-anṣāri","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":6,"ar":"وَٱلَّذِينَ","en_gloss":"and those who","transliteration":"wa-alladhīna","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":7,"ar":"ٱتَّبَعُوهُم","en_gloss":"followed them","transliteration":"ittabaʿūhum","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":8,"ar":"بِإِحْسَـٰنٍۢ","en_gloss":"in righteousness","transliteration":"bi-iḥ'sānin","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":9,"ar":"رَّضِىَ","en_gloss":"Allah is pleased","transliteration":"raḍiya","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":10,"ar":"ٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"Allah is pleased","transliteration":"l-lahu","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":11,"ar":"عَنْهُمْ","en_gloss":"with them","transliteration":"ʿanhum","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":12,"ar":"وَرَضُوا۟","en_gloss":"and they are pleased","transliteration":"waraḍū","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":13,"ar":"عَنْهُ","en_gloss":"with Him","transliteration":"ʿanhu","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":14,"ar":"وَأَعَدَّ","en_gloss":"And He has prepared","transliteration":"wa-aʿadda","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":15,"ar":"لَهُمْ","en_gloss":"for them","transliteration":"lahum","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":16,"ar":"جَنَّـٰتٍۢ","en_gloss":"Gardens","transliteration":"jannātin","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":17,"ar":"تَجْرِى","en_gloss":"flows","transliteration":"tajrī","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":18,"ar":"تَحْتَهَا","en_gloss":"underneath it","transliteration":"taḥtahā","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":19,"ar":"ٱلْأَنْهَـٰرُ","en_gloss":"the rivers","transliteration":"l-anhāru","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":20,"ar":"خَـٰلِدِينَ","en_gloss":"will abide","transliteration":"khālidīna","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":21,"ar":"فِيهَآ","en_gloss":"in it","transliteration":"fīhā","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":22,"ar":"أَبَدًۭا ۚ","en_gloss":"forever","transliteration":"abadan","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":23,"ar":"ذَٰلِكَ","en_gloss":"That","transliteration":"dhālika","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":24,"ar":"ٱلْفَوْزُ","en_gloss":"(is) the success","transliteration":"l-fawzu","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":25,"ar":"ٱلْعَظِيمُ","en_gloss":"the great","transliteration":"l-ʿaẓīmu","verse_key":"9:100"},{"pos":26,"ar":"١٠٠","en_gloss":"(100)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"9:100"}]},{"verse_key":"9:101","surah":9,"ayah":101,"ar_uthmani":"وَمِمَّنْ حَوْلَكُم مِّنَ ٱلْأَعْرَابِ مُنَـٰفِقُونَ ۖ وَمِنْ أَهْلِ ٱلْمَدِينَةِ ۖ مَرَدُوا۟ عَلَى ٱلنِّفَاقِ لَا تَعْلَمُهُمْ ۖ نَحْنُ نَعْلَمُهُمْ ۚ سَنُعَذِّبُهُم مَّرَّتَيْنِ ثُمَّ يُرَدُّونَ إِلَىٰ عَذَابٍ عَظِيمٍ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Some of the desert Arabs around you are hypocrites, as are some of the people of Medina- they are obstinate in their hypocrisy. You [Prophet] do not know them, but We know them well: We shall punish them twice and then they will be returned to [face] a painful punishment [in the Hereafter].","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَمِمَّنْ","en_gloss":"And among those","transliteration":"wamimman","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":2,"ar":"حَوْلَكُم","en_gloss":"around you","transliteration":"ḥawlakum","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":3,"ar":"مِّنَ","en_gloss":"of","transliteration":"mina","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":4,"ar":"ٱلْأَعْرَابِ","en_gloss":"the bedouins","transliteration":"l-aʿrābi","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":5,"ar":"مُنَـٰفِقُونَ ۖ","en_gloss":"(are) hypocrites","transliteration":"munāfiqūna","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":6,"ar":"وَمِنْ","en_gloss":"and (also) from","transliteration":"wamin","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":7,"ar":"أَهْلِ","en_gloss":"people","transliteration":"ahli","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":8,"ar":"ٱلْمَدِينَةِ ۖ","en_gloss":"(of) the Madinah","transliteration":"l-madīnati","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":9,"ar":"مَرَدُوا۟","en_gloss":"They persist","transliteration":"maradū","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":10,"ar":"عَلَى","en_gloss":"in","transliteration":"ʿalā","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":11,"ar":"ٱلنِّفَاقِ","en_gloss":"the hypocrisy","transliteration":"l-nifāqi","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":12,"ar":"لَا","en_gloss":"not","transliteration":"lā","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":13,"ar":"تَعْلَمُهُمْ ۖ","en_gloss":"you know them","transliteration":"taʿlamuhum","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":14,"ar":"نَحْنُ","en_gloss":"We","transliteration":"naḥnu","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":15,"ar":"نَعْلَمُهُمْ ۚ","en_gloss":"[We] know them","transliteration":"naʿlamuhum","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":16,"ar":"سَنُعَذِّبُهُم","en_gloss":"We will punish them","transliteration":"sanuʿadhibuhum","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":17,"ar":"مَّرَّتَيْنِ","en_gloss":"twice","transliteration":"marratayni","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":18,"ar":"ثُمَّ","en_gloss":"then","transliteration":"thumma","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":19,"ar":"يُرَدُّونَ","en_gloss":"they will be returned","transliteration":"yuraddūna","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":20,"ar":"إِلَىٰ","en_gloss":"to","transliteration":"ilā","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":21,"ar":"عَذَابٍ","en_gloss":"a punishment","transliteration":"ʿadhābin","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":22,"ar":"عَظِيمٍۢ","en_gloss":"great","transliteration":"ʿaẓīmin","verse_key":"9:101"},{"pos":23,"ar":"١٠١","en_gloss":"(101)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"9:101"}]},{"verse_key":"9:102","surah":9,"ayah":102,"ar_uthmani":"وَءَاخَرُونَ ٱعْتَرَفُوا۟ بِذُنُوبِهِمْ خَلَطُوا۟ عَمَلًا صَـٰلِحًا وَءَاخَرَ سَيِّئًا عَسَى ٱللَّهُ أَن يَتُوبَ عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"And there are others who have confessed their wrongdoing, who have done some righteous deeds and some bad ones: God may well accept their repentance, for God is most forgiving and merciful.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَءَاخَرُونَ","en_gloss":"And others","transliteration":"waākharūna","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":2,"ar":"ٱعْتَرَفُوا۟","en_gloss":"(who have) acknowledged","transliteration":"iʿ'tarafū","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":3,"ar":"بِذُنُوبِهِمْ","en_gloss":"their sins","transliteration":"bidhunūbihim","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":4,"ar":"خَلَطُوا۟","en_gloss":"They had mixed","transliteration":"khalaṭū","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":5,"ar":"عَمَلًۭا","en_gloss":"a deed","transliteration":"ʿamalan","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":6,"ar":"صَـٰلِحًۭا","en_gloss":"righteous","transliteration":"ṣāliḥan","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":7,"ar":"وَءَاخَرَ","en_gloss":"(with) other","transliteration":"waākhara","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":8,"ar":"سَيِّئًا","en_gloss":"(that was) evil","transliteration":"sayyi-an","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":9,"ar":"عَسَى","en_gloss":"Perhaps","transliteration":"ʿasā","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":10,"ar":"ٱللَّهُ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-lahu","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":11,"ar":"أَن","en_gloss":"[that]","transliteration":"an","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":12,"ar":"يَتُوبَ","en_gloss":"will turn (in mercy)","transliteration":"yatūba","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":13,"ar":"عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ","en_gloss":"to them","transliteration":"ʿalayhim","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":14,"ar":"إِنَّ","en_gloss":"Indeed","transliteration":"inna","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":15,"ar":"ٱللَّهَ","en_gloss":"Allah","transliteration":"l-laha","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":16,"ar":"غَفُورٌۭ","en_gloss":"(is) Oft-Forgiving","transliteration":"ghafūrun","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":17,"ar":"رَّحِيمٌ","en_gloss":"Most Merciful","transliteration":"raḥīmun","verse_key":"9:102"},{"pos":18,"ar":"١٠٢","en_gloss":"(102)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"9:102"}]},{"verse_key":"9:103","surah":9,"ayah":103,"ar_uthmani":"خُذْ مِنْ أَمْوَٰلِهِمْ صَدَقَةً تُطَهِّرُهُمْ وَتُزَكِّيهِم بِهَا وَصَلِّ عَلَيْهِمْ ۖ إِنَّ صَلَوٰتَكَ سَكَنٌ لَّهُمْ ۗ وَٱللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"In order to cleanse and purify them [Prophet], accept a gift out of their property [to make amends] and pray for them- your prayer will be a comfort to them. God is all hearing, all knowing.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"خُذْ","en_gloss":"Take","transliteration":"khudh","verse_key":"9:103"},{"pos":2,"ar":"مِنْ","en_gloss":"from","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"9:103"},{"pos":3,"ar":"أَمْوَٰلِهِمْ","en_gloss":"their wealth","transliteration":"amwālihim","verse_key":"9:103"},{"pos":4,"ar":"صَدَقَةًۭ","en_gloss":"a charity","transliteration":"ṣadaqatan","verse_key":"9:103"},{"pos":5,"ar":"تُطَهِّرُهُمْ","en_gloss":"purifying them","transliteration":"tuṭahhiruhum","verse_key":"9:103"},{"pos":6,"ar":"وَتُزَكِّيهِم","en_gloss":"and cause them increase","transliteration":"watuzakkīhim","verse_key":"9:103"},{"pos":7,"ar":"بِهَا","en_gloss":"by it","transliteration":"bihā","verse_key":"9:103"},{"pos":8,"ar":"وَصَلِّ","en_gloss":"and bless","transliteration":"waṣalli","verse_key":"9:103"},{"pos":9,"ar":"عَلَيْهِمْ ۖ","en_gloss":"[upon] them","transliteration":"ʿalayhim","verse_key":"9:103"},{"pos":10,"ar":"إِنَّ","en_gloss":"Indeed","transliteration":"inna","verse_key":"9:103"},{"pos":11,"ar":"صَلَوٰتَكَ","en_gloss":"your blessings","transliteration":"ṣalataka","verse_key":"9:103"},{"pos":12,"ar":"سَكَنٌۭ","en_gloss":"(are a) reassurance","transliterat